    "definitions": {
      "short": "to be destitute",
      "usage": "lack, needy, (make self) poor (man).",
      "full": "H7326. rush רָאשׁ poor , רֵאשׁ poverty , see רושׁ . [ רוּשׁ or רִישׁ ] 24 verb be in want, poor (related to ירשׁ [compare Qal 3, Niph`al Hiph`il 3 ]? so Thes); — Qal Perfect 3plural וְרָעֵ֑בוּ רָשׁוּ כְּפִירִים Psa 34:11 young lions are in want and hunger ; elsewhere Participle רָשׁ 1Sam 18:23 16 t., רָאשׁ 2Sam 12:1-2 t.; plural רָשִׁים Prov 22:7 , רָאשִׁים 13:23 ; &#8212; (often opposed to עָשִׁיר ): as adjective 1Sam 18:23 ; 2Sam 12:1 , 4 ; Prov 28:3 ; Eccl 4:14 ; as substantive = poor man ( men ), 2Sam 12:3 ; Psa 82:3 ; Eccl 5:7 , especially Prov 10:4 ; 13:8 , 23 12 t. Proverbs. Hithpo`lel Participle מִתְרוֺשֵׁשׁ Prov 13:7 one impoverishing himself (opposed to מִתְעַשֵּׁר ; compare Pô'l. רושׁשׁ Ecclus 11:12; Ecclus 13:5). &#8212; Jer 5:17 ; Mal 1:4 see רשׁשׁ . p. 439f",
